@anupama.b.r1@ibm.com Some fundamental issue. When API is setting error codes why it needs to return a boolean? Error code itself can give info that it was not found or failed.
Also, that is what your statements tells in the Todo "return false and update o_errCode".

@souvikroyofficial10@gmail.com What are we benefiting from moving to std::Expected here?

* We still need to create a variable to hold the value returned in std::expected?

IMO std::expected is best suited when the return values are exclusive not when they mean same thing.

Can you please explain what is the purpose of creating this new API?

This API is doing two tasks:
1. "Checks whether a redundant EEPROM path is defined in the system config JSON"
2. "If present, invokes the VPD collection on the redundant EEPROM path."

This can be handled by below block:
```
if(const auto l_redundantEepromPath = jsonUtility::getRedundantEepromPathFromJson() ; !l_redundantEepromPath.empty())
{
   parseVpdFile();
 }
 ```
